<title>CANADA: Government of Canada sells no gold in January.</title>
<headline>Government of Canada sells no gold in January.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada did not sell any gold in January, leaving reserves at 3.1 million ounces as of January 31.</p>
<p>The Canadian government has a policy of gradually selling off its gold reserves and replacing them with interest-bearing assets.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
